login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf"}]},{"sha":"ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","node_id":"C_kwDOUN_fV9oAKGVjYmQwZWYxMzEwYzFjNjBjZjRhZjEwMmQzOWYxM2FlYjI3YjlhZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-05T13:18:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-05T13:18:01Z"},"message":"Show the top ten, and unblock a survey on a repo whose CI is not green\n\nTwo fixes, both surfaced by the survey run that scored PatelHem.\n\nThe vault now displays the ten highest composites rather than every entry.\nThe cut is by composite, so it is the same arithmetic as the class: improve a\nrepository and it climbs on the next survey. The full catalogue is unchanged\nand still served at /dossier.json, and the plate says how many are below the\ncut rather than quietly dropping them.\n\nThe CI detector in lib/evidence.ts matched only Herald's green rendering\n(\"...runs on every push, green on the last run\"). Herald emits a second one,\n\"Continuous integration is configured.\", when the last run did not succeed.\nEvery repository in the catalogue was green until PatelHem arrived, so the\ngap was invisible until a new repo hit it — and then unmatchedClaims() failed\nthe test gate and blocked the survey from committing. Matching the shared\nprefix fixes it, which is what `container` already did for its two renderings.\n\nAdded a test that pins both alternates of every two-way template, so the next\none fails at desk instead of in the workflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a2152e9e30c19d8c66f87ed5b030b83421a9edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/trees/5a2152e9e30c19d8c66f87ed5b030b83421a9edf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/commits/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/ecbd0ef1310c1c60cf4af102d39f13aeb27b9adf/comments","author":{"login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc"}]},{"sha":"8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","node_id":"C_kwDOUN_fV9oAKDgzNTA1NTk4OTRmMWY0MTc0OGUwM2Q2Y2I0ZTY0M2FkODE4ZjUzY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T11:15:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T11:15:20Z"},"message":"Freeze the regression fixture so a survey can publish\n\nThe first survey run collected cleanly, scored six repositories and composed\nthe catalogue — then failed the test gate and refused to commit. The gate was\nright to stop; the test was wrong.\n\nregression.test.ts read phase00/out/raw.json, which is exactly the file the\nsurvey overwrites with a fresh collection. So it compared today's account\nagainst expectations pinned to 2026-08-26 and broke on changes that were all\ncorrect: vakil gained a commit (27 -> 28) and PatelHem appeared as a sixth\nentry. Six assertions failed without a line of engine code moving, and a valid\nreading could not reach the site.\n\nA regression test pins CODE against KNOWN INPUT. If the input moves with the\naccount it is not a regression test, it is a diff against yesterday. The\nfixture is now a committed copy the survey never touches.\n\nRe-pinning is deliberate: overwrite the fixture and update the numbers in the\nsame commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edf537080fc2f47c9abdfade6a16e1975ace4aef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/trees/edf537080fc2f47c9abdfade6a16e1975ace4aef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/commits/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc/comments","author":{"login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972"}]},{"sha":"a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","node_id":"C_kwDOUN_fV9oAKGExYmMzODhhNjBhYzcwMmRhOTQ4NTliNDU2ZjQ1N2M4YTczNGM5NzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T09:27:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T09:27:27Z"},"message":"Add the survey workflow, a dispatch button, and .gitattributes\n\nThe workflow described in CLAUDE.md did not exist. It does now:\nworkflow_dispatch only, no schedule — a catalogue that rewrites itself nightly\nmakes `generated` meaningless and every commit it produces is noise.\n\nTwo things the workflow has to get right:\n\n  - phase00/gh.mjs caches every API response to disk and returns the file on\n    the next read, and that cache is committed. A run that left it in place\n    would replay a survey from August and report it as today's. The cache is\n    cleared before collecting, which is what makes this an actual reading.\n\n  - the engine and pipeline test suites run before the commit step, so a\n    survey that produced a broken catalogue fails instead of publishing it.\n\nThe site links to the workflow rather than POSTing to it. Firing a workflow\nneeds a token with `actions: write`; behind a public endpoint that would let\nany visitor spend the account's Actions minutes and push commits here.\n\n.gitattributes is unrelated but was found the hard way: autocrlf had checked\nout tokens.css and system.test.ts as CRLF, which broke the contrast parser\n(it matches a two-line selector) and stopped a test file parsing. Both were\nsilent until the tooling ran. An engine meant to be reproducible by anyone\nwho clones it has to include its line endings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b80d7cdf6a2c0936734f9f4b0f11e8a807d58c80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/trees/b80d7cdf6a2c0936734f9f4b0f11e8a807d58c80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/git/commits/a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/commits/a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60/PatelHem/commit/a1bc388a60ac702da94859b456f457c8a734c972","comments_url":"